==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ḱel- (cover)}}
Probably denominal, perhaps from {{m|itc-pro||*kēlā|t=concealment}} or from a root noun {{m|itc-pro||*kēls}}, ultimately from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ḱel-}}. The lengthened grade reminds of Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*hēliz}}, the etymon of Old High German {{m|goh|hāli}}. The older and more straightforward formation {{m|itc-pro||*kelō}} is found in {{m|la|occulō}}.

Cognate to {{cog|la|clam}}, {{cog|sga|ceilid|t=to hide}} and {{cog|gem-pro|*helaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*huljaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cēlō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+.p3inf.poet-sync-perf|cēlō}}

# to [[hide]] (something from someone), [[cover]], [[keep]] a [[secret]], [[conceal]]
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs|12|23|quote=Homō versūtus '''cēlat''' scientiam: et cor īnsipientium prōvocābit stultitiam.|trans=''A cautious man '''concealeth [conceals]''' knowledge: and the heart of fools publisheth folly.'' (Douay-Rheims trans., Challoner rev.: '''1752''' CE)}}

